==English==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|en|enm|westen}}, from {{inh|en|ang|wēsten||a desert, waste}}, from {{inh|en|gem-pro|*wōstinjō||a waste, wilderness}}, from {{inh|en|ine-pro|*wāsto-||empty, wasted}}. Cognate with {{cog|fy|woastyn||desert}}, {{cog|stq|wustenej||desert}}, {{cog|nl|woestijn||desert}}, {{cog|fr|gâtine||wasteland, moor}} (from {{cog|gem}}), {{cog|gmh|wuostinne||desert, wilderness}} ({{cog|de|Wüste||desert}}). More at {{l|en|westy}}, {{l|en|waste}}.

{{PIE root|en|h₁weh₂}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{lb|en|obsolete}} A [[waste]], [[wasteland]]; [[desert]].

===Anagrams===
* {{anagrams|en|a=eenstw|Wentes|newest|newset|tweens}}

